and we especially love
talented dogs

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:06.501
and we found some very talented
dogs that we want you to meet.

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:08.968
It's time for "What's Up Dog
Sports Edition"

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:10.400
♪ What's Up Dog? ♪

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:11.834
♪ What's Up Dog? ♪

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.501
♪ What's Up Dog? ♪

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:15.000
♪ What's Up Dog? ♪

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.234
-Sports Edition!

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:19.567
-Welcome to "What's Up Dog?
Sports Edition."

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:20.834
Let's meet our first dog

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:23.033
and find out what sport
they're playing.

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:24.801
[ Cheering and applause ]
Hi. Nice to see you.

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:26.501
What is your name?
-Yannick Devost.

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:28.701
-Hey, Yannick.
Who'd you bring with us today?

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:29.901
-Maggie.
-Hi, Maggie!

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:31.334
-[ Whimpering ]
-What kind of dog is Maggie?

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:34.601
-A German shepherd.
-A German shepherd. Maggie.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.434
What sport does Maggie
play here?

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:38.367
I'm assuming hockey?
-Yep, hockey.

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:39.968
She's a real life hockey goalie.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.334
-She's a hockey goalie.
Alright. She's excited now.

00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:43.801
[ Laughter ]
Oh, look, she's getting ready.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:46.534
Now, what is the trick,
she just blocks all the shots?

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:49.968
-No. So, she only focuses
on the puck.

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:52.667
I'll try to distract her
by shooting all the balls.

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:56.033
She'll ignore them, and she'll
only focus on the puck.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:58.067
-I got to see this.
Alright, Maggie,

00:00:58.067 --> 00:00:59.501
you're in the net.
You're ready to go.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.934
Roots [indistinct]
-Can you hold on to that for me?

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.868
-Sure, of course.
-Goalie.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:05.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:07.434
[ Ohhs ]

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.300
[ Awws ]

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:18.767
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:21.033
[ Rimshot ]
-What?!

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:25.033
Wow! Wow! Wow! Wow! Wow!

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:26.734
That was awesome!

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:28.200
Maggie!

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.801
Can we see that in slow-motion?

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.567
That's great.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:33.901
Oh, my gosh!
Look at that. Watch this.

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:35.367
[ Laughter ]
Ow! Chomps!

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:36.901
Good job!

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:38.367
Great job, buddy.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:39.901
Thank you so much.
You can head over there.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:41.467
-Thank you.
-Yannick, tank you very much
for being here.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.067
Go on, Maggie.
Thank you very much.

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:47.033
Alright,
let's meet our next dog

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.467
and find out what sport
they are playing.

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:50.501
Come on over, guys.

00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:51.667
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.701
-How are you, Jim?

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:54.901
-Pleasure.
-I'm Dave.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:56.300
-Jimmy. Hey, Dave.
-I'm Dan.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.567
-Hey, Dan.
Nice to meet you guys.

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:59.000
And who's this?
-This is Pepper.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.334
-[ Baby voice ] Hi, Pepper!
Nice to see you.

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:03.601
Pepper. Now, Pepper --
what kind of dog is Pepper?

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:05.234
She's an Australian cattle dog.

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:07.367
-An Australian cattle dog.
She's very excited.

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:08.968
-Oh, she's fired up,
ready to go.

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:10.400
-You're holding
two sports things,

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.901
so I don't know
what sport she plays.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:14.133
-Kind of a Wiffle
hockey baseball.

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:16.000
-Wickey --
Wiffle hockey baseball.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.501
-Yes.
-That's what Pepper enjoys?

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:19.501
-That's what she's into.
-Yeah.

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:22.067
And how does this work?
-Well, she holds the bat,

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:24.000
I hit the ball to her
with the hockey stick,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.033
and she hits it.

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:25.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:27.167
-Hopefully.
Hopefully.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:28.534
-What do you mean, hopefully?
It's going to work.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:30.734
This'll be great. Alright.
What can I do to help, anything?

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:31.934
Just get out of the way?
-Duck.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.067
[ Laughter ]
-Okay, yeah.

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:36.934
Good man. Good man.
Alright, cool. Perfect.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:37.901
You want to just give her
the bat...

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:38.934
-Here we go.
-...and go for it?

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.434
[ Drumroll ]
Okay.
-Ready?

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:43.467
[ Audience murmuring ]
Alright.

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:45.267
Get in your spot right here.

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:46.367
Stay there.
Stay.

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:49.234
[ Playing whimsical
suspenseful tune ]

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:52.267
♪♪

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:54.601
Got to trash talk sometimes.
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.501
-You can't hit.
You're a dog.

00:02:56.501 --> 00:02:57.667
[ Laughter ]
Ready?

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:00.734
-Oh.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.334
-Strike one!

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:06.868
[ Laughter ]
Come on, Pepper!
You got this one!

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:08.033
-Come on, Pepper!

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:09.367
-I think she believed me --
she couldn't hit.

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:11.801
She's a dog.
Ready?

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.667
-Oh!
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:18.100
That's pretty good.
That's pretty good.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.434
[ Rimshot ]
I'll take that.

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:21.968
Can we see that in slow-motion?
I like that.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.567
It was a swing.
She swung at it.

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:24.934
Look at -- what?

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:27.367
Yes! Alright, good.
I'll take that.

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:28.567
Thank you very much
for being here.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:29.801
I appreciate it.
Pepper, thank you.

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:31.701
Thank you very much.
Thank you, Pepper.

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:33.834
Thank you, Pepper.
Take care.

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:35.434
[ Laughter ]
Alright, Pepper. Take care.

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:37.767
Alright,
let's meet our last dog.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:39.868
Come on over here.
What's your name?

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:40.701
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:42.834
Hey.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:42.834 --> 00:03:44.501
Wow. Cool.

00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:46.701
The dog just skateboarded in.
That was awesome.

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:48.901
Was that the trick?
-Part of it.

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.367
-Yeah, that was amazing.
Hi. Jimmy.

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:53.334
-Hi. Chrissy.
-Hi, Chrissy. Hi. Jimmy.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:55.701
[ Cheering and applause ]
-This is Kevin.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.100
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.968
-Good job.

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:01.400
-That's awesome.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.601
[ Awws ]
Oh, wow!
What a beautiful little --

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:05.100
What?
What kind of dog?

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.968
-He's a. border collie.
-He's a border collie.

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:08.701
-What is his name again?
-Kevin Bacon.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:10.434
[ Laughter ]
-Kev--

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:12.534
There you go.
I'm a big fan, Kevin.

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:14.100
-Come say hi.
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.767
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Good job, bud.

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:17.501
-What does Kevin Bacon do?

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:19.067
-So, he's a huge helper
around the house,

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:22.467
